  "tool_classification_limit": "Lexical direct calls and structured responses; nested invocations may be missed. Repeated hash does not itself prove unnecessary work.",
  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the brief, feedback, notes, and current backend, then target the observed failures and measured bottlenecks. I\u2019ll run the relevant checks and stop any test servers I start. I\u2019m also applying the installed OpenSocrates guidance for the judgment calls in this follow-up.",
    "The feedback shows one correctness failure: a migrated version 1 idempotency key accepts a request that explicitly adds a new scheduling field at its default value. The replay check currently compares normalized values, which loses whether that field was present. I\u2019ll preserve ordinary version 2 default equivalence and narrow only the legacy replay check. The load data is diagnostic because correctness failed and the measured run did not complete; it does not justify a throughput claim.",
    "The targeted fix is in place, and `go test -race ./...` plus the required build pass. I\u2019m checking the other side of the boundary now: a new version 2 key should still replay when omitted scheduling fields are later supplied with their defaults. I\u2019ll record the feedback\u2019s load limit in the docs and notes.",
    "The regression checks now pass on both sides of the replay rule: migrated version 1 keys reject explicit version 2 fields, while new version 2 keys still accept equivalent defaults. Source review found potentially costly whole-tenant counts and claim reconciliation under the write lock, but the available load result did not isolate either as a bottleneck. I\u2019ve left those paths and the WAL/FULL durability settings intact.",
    "Fixed the migrated version 1 idempotency replay failure. [service.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queueforge/service.go:385) now rejects an explicitly added version 2 scheduling field under an original version 1 key, even when its value is the default. New version 2 keys still treat omitted and explicit defaults as equivalent. I added regression cases in [followup_test.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queueforge/followup_test.go:157) and updated the [README](<WORKSPACE>/README.md) and [project notes](<WORKSPACE>/PROJECT_NOTES.md).\n\nGo 1.26.3 `go test -race ./...`, the required build, and `git diff --check` pass. The independent frozen API and load checks have **not** been rerun on this repair. Their earlier load result failed its correctness gate and does not establish a throughput gain, so I made no speculative storage optimization. I started no server process. OpenSocrates native activation was unconfirmed; no canonical method was applied."
  ],
